# Cairo Dependency and Presentation Assertion Cleanup

Purpose:
    Remove tests of incidental presentation details and eliminate unnecessary
    native Cairo dependencies while preserving meaningful behavioral coverage.
    This is an implementation task list, not a claim that the cleanup is complete.

Scope and constraints:
    - Review VanillaExpanded.Tests, its shared fixtures, necessary production
      seams, dependency configuration, CI, and directly related documentation.
    - Do not preserve an assertion merely because it already exists.
    - Do not replace pixel assertions with equivalent checks of style constants,
      drawing commands, decorative coordinates, or internal implementation details.
    - Preserve activation, selection, callbacks, focus, scrolling, state restoration,
      input routing, clipping correctness, and resource ownership where applicable.
    - Distinguish decorative geometry from functional geometry such as hit targets,
      reachable controls, viewport containment, and scroll limits.
    - Keep game reference sources read-only. Avoid production rendering changes
      unless a small, justified seam is necessary for behavioral testing.
    - Prefer eliminating native Cairo from all retained tests. Do not assume a
      permanent Cairo-backed test lane is required.

## Phase 1: Confirm policy boundaries and inventory
    Prerequisite: none.
    Policy confirmed by the user: no pixel-output or presentation-only exceptions,
    including whole-buffer non-modification. Functional geometry is permitted when
    tied to hit testing, clipping, viewport containment, reachability, and scroll limits.
    Decision record: [CairoTestInventory](CairoTestInventory.md).
    [x] Confirm and document any allowed exceptions to the user's policies against
        pixel-output and presentation-detail assertions before retaining such tests.
        No exceptions are approved.
    [x] Inventory assertions across the test project, including shared assertion
        helpers, captured textures, surface buffers, sampled channels, and alpha.
    [x] Include non-pixel presentation assertions: palette values, font sizes,
        decorative spacing, exact styling dimensions, and rendering command values.
    [x] Classify each suspect assertion as presentation-only, meaningful behavior,
        or a mixed/ambiguous contract; resolve ambiguous cases against requirements.
    [x] Trace native Cairo entry points separately from assertion policy: font
        initialization, text measurement, real composition, text texture generation,
        and fixtures that initialize these incidentally.
    [x] Record decisions by test method and shared fixture, including behavior to
        preserve and any approved exception. Do not use test category as a proxy
        for native dependencies.
    Completion:
        Every identified assertion has a disposition and behavioral coverage owner.
        The earlier inventory of 18 methods / 87 declared cases is a starting point,
        not an exhaustive inventory of presentation assertions or Cairo dependencies.

## Phase 2: Remove known Cairo pixel assertions without losing behavior
    Prerequisite: [Phase 1 decisions](CairoTestInventory.md) for each affected batch.
    Apply these tasks to the named methods in the linked files. Remove assertions
    that are presentation-only; preserve or relocate independent behavioral checks.
    Delete whole tests only when no justified contract remains, subject to approved
    exceptions. Rename retained tests to describe their remaining behavior.

    Unit:
    [x] [GuiControlVisualsTests](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Unit/Gui/GuiControlVisualsTests.cs):
        FrameHasApprovedFillAndGuiScaledWholePixelOutline.
        Remove exact fill/outline and rasterized stroke checks.
    [x] [GuiControlVisualsTests](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Unit/Gui/GuiControlVisualsTests.cs):
        GradientsAreLocalAndInvalidPixelGeometryFailsExplicitly.
        Remove gradient endpoint checks; reassess and retain justified input-validation
        coverage independently of surface creation.

    Component GUI:
    [x] [GuiElementIconTabsTests](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Component/Gui/GuiElementIconTabsTests.cs):
        FolderTabRasterHasRoundedShouldersAndOpensIntoTheMatchingPanel.
        Remove shoulder, fill, accent, outline, and panel-edge pixel expectations.
    [x] [GuiStyledControlStateRenderingTests](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Component/Gui/GuiStyledControlStateRenderingTests.cs):
        PopupSelectionPresenceInvalidatesCachedIndicator.
        Remove selection-color searches; retain only justified selection/cache behavior.
    [x] [GuiStyledControlStateRenderingTests](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Component/Gui/GuiStyledControlStateRenderingTests.cs):
        ScrollbarPointerFeedbackTracksCaptureAndCancelsWithoutExtraScrollOrUploads.
        Remove hover/pressed colors and disabled-alpha checks; preserve capture,
        cancellation, scrolling, and justified resource-lifecycle checks.

    Component Recipe Book:
    [x] [RecipeBookDialogLayoutTests](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Component/RecipeBook/RecipeBookDialogLayoutTests.cs):
        BaselineShellAdoptsSharedControlsAndCentersTheRealMultiDigitCounter.
        Remove shell colors, gradients, separators, and decorative placement checks.
        Preserve independently justified functional layout and control wiring.
    [x] [RecipeBookOptionsTests](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Component/RecipeBook/RecipeBookOptionsTests.cs):
        RecipeBookOptionsSvgStatesUseIsolatedTexturesWithoutModifyingTheSharedDialogSurface.
        Whole-buffer non-modification is not an approved exception.
        Replace only with meaningful isolation/ownership coverage.

    Integration styled controls:
    [x] [GuiStyledControlsNativeCompatibilityTests](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Integration/Gui/GuiStyledControlsNativeCompatibilityTests.cs):
        ButtonPreservesNativeActivationAndRendersApprovedStates.
        Remove state colors and text-alpha checks; preserve activation and disabled behavior.
    [x] [GuiStyledControlsNativeCompatibilityTests](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Integration/Gui/GuiStyledControlsNativeCompatibilityTests.cs):
        ClearableInputUsesCallerLabelsAndNotifiesExactlyOnceWithNativeGeometry.
        Remove fill, placeholder color/opacity, and decorative inset checks; preserve
        editing, clear notification, focus, and functional hit geometry.
    [x] [GuiStyledControlsNativeCompatibilityTests](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Integration/Gui/GuiStyledControlsNativeCompatibilityTests.cs):
        DropdownCachesStyledResourcesAcrossNativeOpeningReplacementAndSelection.
        Remove field/popup colors, selection pixels, alpha, and buffer comparisons;
        preserve opening, replacement, selection, and resource ownership behavior.
    [x] [GuiStyledControlsNativeCompatibilityTests](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Integration/Gui/GuiStyledControlsNativeCompatibilityTests.cs):
        CheckboxHasFlatScaledFrameNativeTogglingAndDisabledIndicator.
        Remove frame colors and indicator alpha; preserve toggling and disabled behavior.
    [x] [GuiStyledControlsNativeCompatibilityTests](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Integration/Gui/GuiStyledControlsNativeCompatibilityTests.cs):
        ScrollbarArrowsAndInsetThumbShareNativeRangeAndReleaseDragOutside.
        Remove track/thumb colors, corner transparency, and arrow alpha; preserve
        range handling, dragging, boundary behavior, and release outside the control.
    [x] [GuiStyledControlsNativeCompatibilityTests](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Integration/Gui/GuiStyledControlsNativeCompatibilityTests.cs):
        ArrowButtonsUseNativeMomentaryActivationWithoutExtraFocusOrReleaseCallbacks.
        Remove hover-color checks; preserve momentary activation, focus, and callback semantics.

    Integration native probes:
    [x] [GuiControlNativeProbeTests](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Integration/Gui/GuiControlNativeProbeTests.cs):
        BorderlessButtonRetainsNativeActivationAndVisibilityWithLocalFlatChrome.
