## Phase 3: Complete the presentation-policy cleanup
    Prerequisite: Phase 1 inventory; may proceed alongside Phase 2 in disjoint files.
    [ ] Resolve remaining presentation assertions found beyond the 18-method inventory.
    [ ] Reassess palette/constants-only tests and mixed font/metrics tests, including
        [RecipeBookVisualMetricsTests](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Unit/RecipeBook/RecipeBookVisualMetricsTests.cs).
    [ ] Replace decorative positioning assertions only where a genuine functional
        requirement exists; otherwise remove them rather than inventing a substitute.
    [ ] Preserve functional geometry tests for hit testing, clipping, reachability,
        scrolling, and viewport behavior without pinning incidental styling choices.
    [ ] Remove unused raster capture, pixel sampling, appearance-only test probes,
        and dependencies that no longer serve retained coverage.
    Completion:
        No unapproved presentation contracts remain in the reviewed scope, whether
        expressed as pixel bytes, constants, commands, or decorative geometry.

## Phase 4: Decouple retained behavior from native Cairo
    Prerequisite: assertion dispositions for each affected batch.
    [ ] Replace broad menu/composer fixtures with focused fixtures for session state,
        filtering, selection, options persistence, lifecycle, and cache policy.
    [ ] Reuse existing RecipeBookSession, RecipeBookLayout, RecipeBookLayoutCache,
        and RecipeBookIconCache boundaries before introducing new abstractions.
    [ ] Remove real TextTextureUtil, font creation, and eager composition from fixtures
        whose remaining behavioral contracts do not require them.
    [ ] Drive icon scheduling, request budgets, completion, reload, and disposal through
        mocked atlas/render boundaries without unrelated text or tile composition.
    [ ] Evaluate separating measured text inputs from layout arithmetic where necessary;
        keep real font handling in production and avoid hardcoded fake production metrics.
    [ ] Assess remaining real-control input/composition tests individually. Preserve
        functional wiring coverage rather than replacing every real collaborator
        with a mock and claiming equivalent verification.
    [ ] Do not bypass static initialization, fabricate uninitialized engine objects,
        patch native calls globally, or silently swallow library-loading errors.
    [ ] Record each residual Cairo dependency with its retained behavioral purpose.
        Obtain a decision on unresolved cases before retiring meaningful coverage
        or introducing an optional native-backed suite.
    Completion:
        Retained managed tests do not reach native Cairo. Any unavoidable residual
        dependency is explicit and approved, not merely inherited from old fixtures.

## Phase 5: Align configuration, CI, and documentation
    Prerequisite: Phase 4 dependency outcomes.
    [ ] Distinguish native libcairo removal from managed cairo-sharp reference removal.
        Keep assembly references still required by engine signatures or production types.
    [ ] Remove obsolete native test-copy items and fixture dependencies only after
        proving no retained tests require them. Check SkiaSharp separately.
    [ ] Keep Unit/Component/Integration classification based on actual test boundaries;
        preserve required GUI serialization and teardown safeguards.
    [ ] If exceptions are approved, use an explicit capability selector independent
        of test category, and ensure the exceptional tests actually run in CI.
        Do not silently skip failed tests or treat missing libraries as success.
    [ ] Update the existing build/test workflow to exercise the intended dependency-free
        scope and any explicitly approved residual scope without hiding coverage loss.
    [ ] Update directly related test guidance and commands to state the presentation
        policy, approved exceptions, and the final native dependency requirements.
    Completion:
        Project configuration, CI selection, and documentation match the retained
        contracts and do not imply that Category=Unit guarantees Cairo independence.

## Phase 6: Verify behavior and dependency elimination
    Prerequisite: coherent implementation batches from Phases 2-5.
    [ ] Follow the configured test workflow for test writing and independent review;
        reconcile coverage losses and policy exceptions before marking work complete.
    [ ] Run focused changed suites first, then the intended complete test scope.
    [ ] Verify native Cairo independence in a clean process/environment where the
        library cannot be resolved, including through bundled or system search paths.
        Merely deleting the test-output copy or observing a green filtered run is insufficient.
    [ ] Exercise Windows and Linux test paths relevant to the CI failure.
    [ ] Confirm the validation environment actually executes the retained tests;
        report discovery counts, approved removals, skips, and residual dependencies.
    [ ] Check that activation, callbacks, focus, scrolling, restoration, functional
        geometry, event unsubscription, and resource cleanup retain appropriate coverage.
    [ ] Search for residual unapproved pixel/presentation assertions, including indirect
        helper calls, and resolve any remaining native-loading paths.
    [ ] Build/type-check the mod and tests using existing tooling; validate any changed
        production seams without changing game rendering behavior.
    Final completion:
        Presentation-policy cleanup is independently reviewed. Native Cairo is absent
        from all retained tests, or every remaining requirement is explicitly approved
        and verified. No coverage reduction is concealed by filtering or fallback behavior.
